/ `load vars` on a read builds file.read with Template=true, so the file's own %name% is filled from memory
/ before the content is returned. A plain read with no such phrase leaves the text as written (%name% raw).
/ note.txt holds "Hello %name%"; with %name% = "World" the filled read says "Hello World", the plain one does not.
Start
- set %name% = "World"
- read 'note.txt', load vars, write to %filled%
- read 'note.txt', write to %raw%
- assert that %filled% contains "World"
- assert that %raw% does not contain "World"
